<div class="text"><h1>Breakfast....</h1>
<pre><h1>The Overall Role of This Breakfast</h1>
<h3><i>This classic meal is a high-energy, convenient morning fuel plate designed to jumpstart your day quickly without complex cooking.</i></h3>

<h3>Sustained Morning Fuel:</h3> Whole-grain brown bread provides complex carbohydrates that release glucose steadily, keeping brain fog away during morning study or work sessions.

<h3>Long-Lasting Fullness & Healthy Fats:</h3> Peanut butter brings heart-healthy monounsaturated fats and plant protein, slowing down digestion to keep you satisfied until lunch.

<h3>Instant Vitality & Electrolytes:</h3> Bananas supply quick-digesting natural carbs and potassium, helping regulate fluid balance and preventing muscle sluggishness.

<h3>Bone Health & Protein Boost:</h3> Milk completes the meal by adding high-quality dairy protein (casein & whey) along with calcium and Vitamin D.
</pre>
<hr>
<pre><h1>Lunch.....</h1>
<h1>The Overall Role of This Meal</h1>
<h3><i>This dish serves as a comforting, nutrient-dense main meal (ideal for lunch or dinner) that balances high protein with sustained carbohydrates.</i></h3>

<h3>Muscle Repair & Recovery:</h3> The protein core (chicken breast or paneer cubes) delivers amino acids necessary for muscle repair, strength building, and fat loss support.

<h3>Steady Energy Supply:</h3> The rice provides complex carbohydrates to replenish depleted glycogen levels, giving you steady stamina for work, study, or workouts.

<h3>Metabolic Support & Immunity:</h3> The rich curry gravy (typically made with onion, tomato, garlic, ginger, and spices like turmeric) offers natural anti-inflammatory benefits, aids digestion, and boosts immune health.
</pre>
<hr>
<pre><h1>Snack....</h1>
<h1>The Overall Role of This Snack</h1>
<h3><i>This bowl is a quick, natural pre-workout or mid-day energy booster designed to keep you focused and powered up without causing a sugar crash.</i></h3>

<h3>Immediate & Sustained Energy:</h3> Bananas provide fast-acting, easily digestible natural carbs (fructose and glucose) for quick stamina, while almonds supply slow-digesting healthy fats to sustain that energy over hours.

<h3>Muscle & Cramp Protection:</h3> Bananas are rich in potassium and almonds in magnesium, a combination that supports proper nerve function, muscle contraction, and helps prevent muscle cramps during activity.

<h3>Brain & Heart Health:</h3> Whole almonds contain Vitamin E and monounsaturated fats, which aid mental focus and support cardiovascular health.

</pre>
<hr>
<pre><h1>Dinner.........</h1>
<h1>The Overall Role of This Meal</h1>
<h3><i>This bowl is a clean, whole-food dinner designed for efficient nutrient absorption, muscle recovery, and hormone support while keeping digestion light before sleep.</i></h3>

<h3>Complete Protein for Muscle Recovery:</h3> Hard-boiled eggs provide high-quality complete protein containing all essential amino acids to repair tissues overnight.

<h3>Complex Carbs & Fiber:</h3> Roasted sweet potatoes offer slow-digesting, complex carbohydrates that naturally support healthy serotonin levels for restful sleep without spiking insulin.

<h3>Heart-Healthy Fats & Satiety:</h3>Diced avocado delivers monounsaturated fatty acids and dietary fiber, slowing digestion to prevent late-night snack cravings while aiding the absorption of fat-soluble vitamins (A, D, E, K).
</pre>
